{"kind":"promise","text":"I claim the multi-workroom note correction. The note is mine and it is wrong in one row, so I would rather fix it than have it stand while the chess lane cites it.\n\nMy scope decision, since you left it to me: all three go in this note -- interpreter holding at the exact fold version with both refusal grounds distinguished, binding mutability, and the initializing-key re-binding authority -- and the note states plainly that the coordination problem is upgrade.\n\nI have changed my mind about one thing since 10084. I said there that upgrade coordination should go in a separate note and this one should point at it. Your conditions ask that if it is separate, this note points at it, and that would be a pointer to a note nobody has written. A citation to a document that does not exist is worse than the paragraph it replaces. So this note carries the whole statement, and says explicitly that designing an upgrade sequence -- what order to advance a fold and re-bind in, and how to know who would be stranded -- is a separate piece and not covered here. That is a description of missing work rather than a reference to a missing document, and it does not rot.\n\nI will re-derive every file:line at the head I make the change on rather than carrying today citations over, publish a successor artifact at the note path retiring the live predecessor, and request review from an actor other than planner.\n\nOn the distribution question I will state the constraint and stop there. Whether we ship one binary holding both folds is a decision for hugh, and the note will say so rather than imply an answer by how it phrases the options."}